NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" hook can be used to fetch a variable number of queries:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const results = useQueries({\n  queries: [\n    { queryKey: ['post', 1], queryFn: fetchPost, staleTime: Infinity },\n    { queryKey: ['post', 2], queryFn: fetchPost, staleTime: Infinity },\n  ],\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" hook accepts an options object with a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queries"}]},{"type":"text","value":" key whose value is an array with query option objects identical to the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" hook"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (excluding the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" option)."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context?: React.Context<QueryClient | undefined>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this to use a custom React Query context. Otherwise, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultContext"},{"type":"text","value":" will be used."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Having the same query key more than once in the array of query objects may cause some data to be shared between queries, e.g. when using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"placeholderData"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":". To avoid this, consider de-duplicating the queries and map the results back to the desired structure."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" hook returns an array with all the query results. The order returned is the same as the input order."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `useQueries` hook can be used to fetch a variable number of queries:\n\n```tsx\nconst results = useQueries({\n  queries: [\n    { queryKey: ['post', 1], queryFn: fetchPost, staleTime: Infinity },\n    { queryKey: ['post', 2], queryFn: fetchPost, staleTime: Infinity },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n**Options**\n\nThe `useQueries` hook accepts an options object with a **queries** key whose value is an array with query option objects identical to the [`useQuery` hook](../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery) (excluding the `context` option).\n\n- `context?: React.Context<QueryClient | undefined>`\n  - Use this to use a custom React Query context. Otherwise, `defaultContext` will be used.\n\n> Having the same query key more than once in the array of query objects may cause some data to be shared between queries, e.g. when using `placeholderData` and `select`. To avoid this, consider de-duplicating the queries and map the results back to the desired structure.\n\n**Returns**\n\nThe `useQueries` hook returns an array with all the query results. The order returned is the same as the input order.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useQueries\ntitle: useQueries\n---\n\nThe `useQueries` hook can be used to fetch a variable number of queries:\n\n```tsx\nconst results = useQueries({\n  queries: [\n    { queryKey: ['post', 1], queryFn: fetchPost, staleTime: Infinity },\n    { queryKey: ['post', 2], queryFn: fetchPost, staleTime: Infinity },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n**Options**\n\nThe `useQueries` hook accepts an options object with a **queries** key whose value is an array with query option objects identical to the [`useQuery` hook](../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery) (excluding the `context` option).\n\n- `context?: React.Context<QueryClient | undefined>`\n  - Use this to use a custom React Query context. Otherwise, `defaultContext` will be used.\n\n> Having the same query key more than once in the array of query objects may cause some data to be shared between queries, e.g. when using `placeholderData` and `select`. To avoid this, consider de-duplicating the queries and map the results back to the desired structure.\n\n**Returns**\n\nThe `useQueries` hook returns an array with all the query results. The order returned is the same as the input order.\n"}
